# Every branch in a fix batch appends its own line to the journeys changelog,
# so every one of them collides with every other one on the same first line.
# "Keep every entry, from both sides" is exactly what Git's built-in union
# driver does, and it is the right answer for an append-only log: nothing is
# a conflict, nothing is lost, and the file stays newest-at-top because each
# branch appends at the top of its own copy.
#
# Union is correct for a log and WRONG for anything with structure — do not
# extend this to code, JSON, or a file where two halves have to agree.
docs/journeys/CHANGELOG.md merge=union
